# Deferred log -- mandatory for every agent

The repo root file `DEFERRED_LOG.md` is the **parking lot for known bugs and parked features**. It is a peer of `PROBLEM_LOG.md` -- same respect, same Lifecycle declaration, same constitution severity if you skip it after parking real work.

**This rule applies to every agent that works in this repo** -- parent Auto sessions, Cursor built-ins used on Nova work, and every Nova specialist (`tester`, `hod-momo`, `market-feed`, ...). There is no exception by agent type or "we were busy" framing.

## Hard requirement

When a session **finds a real bug it will not fix now**, or **parks a feature the human asked for**, the agent **MUST** prepend (or extend) an entry in `DEFERRED_LOG.md` in the **same session** (before or with the CHANGELOG / task-log / commit):

- A bug whose fix is too big, architectural, or the wrong task for this session
- A fully diagnosed root cause whose patch is deferred (do not band-aid; do not stay silent)
- A user-requested feature you declined to build now (too complicated, needs an ADR, needs a human decision)

**Skipping DEFERRED_LOG after parking real work is a constitution violation** -- same severity as skipping `PROBLEM_LOG.md` after a real fix.

## Before any fix (mandatory, every chat)

**Read this file first** -- before writing a patch, before "quick" UI/tooling work, before telling the human you will fix something.

1. Run `py -3 tools/deferred_log.py status` (alias: `priorities`). The file is repo-root `DEFERRED_LOG.md`. That ranked list **is** the known-bugs / parked-features to-do. When the human asks "what's missing / what are our priorities," answer from this command -- do not invent a second tracker.
2. Search the file for the module, symptom, or keyword. If a `D-NNN` already covers the ask: **work from that entry**. Honor **Status** (`parked` means do not start it), **Unblock**, and **Next**. Do not start a parallel fix that ignores them.
3. If you are about to "improve" chart drawings, scanners, VWAP, lifespan, NEWS, or any other named row: you must cite the matching `D-NNN` or explain why this is a different bug.

Starting a fix that is already written on this page, without reading the page, is a constitution violation -- same class as parking work with no entry.

Search `DEFERRED_LOG.md` (and `py -3 tools/deferred_log.py status`) before dumping a new item. Extend an existing `D-NNN` when the same gap is rediscovered.

## Where and how

1. Open items: prepend a new `## D-NNN` section immediately below `<!-- OPEN_START -->`. Next ID: `py -3 tools/deferred_log.py next-id`.
2. Use the template in `DEFERRED_LOG.md`. Severity, Effort, Why parked, Blast radius, Unblock, Next, and Evidence are never optional.
3. Do not log secrets, tokens, or personal data.
4. Cross-link from CHANGELOG / task-log `Related:` when those also get an entry.
5. When you later **fix** it: move the section to Closed, write `PROBLEM_LOG.md` if it was a bug, and set Lifecycle `deferred_log=D-NNN` plus `problem_log=...`.

## Do not

- Dump parked work only into `.cursor/agent-memory/*-memory.md` Backlog (scratchpad, not SSOT)
- Dump product-phase NEXT / L-Z parking-lot work here -- that stays in `Nova-Roadmap-Status.md`
- Treat a CHANGELOG `Follow-ups:` bullet as enough -- if it is a real bug or parked feature, it belongs here
- Band-aid a P0/P1 so you can skip writing the entry
- Invent an ID; never reuse a Closed ID
- Start a fix that is already a `D-NNN` without reading that entry first (honor `parked` / Unblock / Next)

## When skip is allowed

Only for:

- You actually **fixed** the bug this session (that is `PROBLEM_LOG.md`, then `deferred_log=none` unless you also closed a D-NNN)
- Purely cosmetic edits with nothing parked
- Status-only polls / read-only triage with no new gap found
- The gap is already an open `D-NNN` and you did not learn anything new -- still declare `deferred_log=D-NNN` if you touched that area, else `none`

When skipping, Lifecycle (specialists) or the closing report (parent) **MUST** say `deferred_log=none`, `deferred_log=skipped`, or `deferred_log=n/a` -- never silently omit the declaration.

## Lifecycle declaration (specialists + parent reports that use Lifecycle)

Every Lifecycle footer **MUST** include:

```text
deferred_log=<D-NNN>|none|skipped|n/a
```

Example after parking a bug:

```text
**Lifecycle:** memory=changed | promotion=none | dashboard=clean | handoff=none | task_log=knowledge/task-log/2026-08-26-example.md | problem_log=n/a | deferred_log=D-001
```

## Relationship to other logs

| Log | Answers |
|-----|---------|
| `PROBLEM_LOG.md` | What went wrong and how it was **fixed** |
| `DEFERRED_LOG.md` | What is **still wrong or not built**, with severity so a human can prioritize |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | What the codebase does now |
| `knowledge/task-log/` | Full job narrative + why this approach |
| `Nova-Roadmap-Status.md` | Product phase NEXT (not a bug tracker) |

